Z||000000||86SE||08-17-2001||08:49 PM||||I was at advance Auto and I bought a Flywheel for a '88 Fiero V-6 for my 3.4 conversion.  The computer said it was a flywheel/flexplate.  I told the guy its for an auto.  I picked up the part the next week.  On the box it has a picture of a flexplate which looked like an oddly shaped square.  Then i flywheel which was a circle with a ring gear around it.  I opened the box and it was a flywheel, but i dident see a square flexplate.  Nothing is bolted or welded (except for the ring gear) onto it.<P>Is this  the flexplate I need for an Automatic trans, or is it a flywheel for the manual??  It has a bunch of different holes in it so maybe my '86 flexplate can bolt onto it??<P>Im confused, any help would be appreciated.<P>Chuck||||reg||11
Z||000001||Chris McDonald||08-17-2001||09:04 PM||||Flexplate is for an automatic transmission and it has a lot of holes in it.<P>A Flywheel is heavy, thick, and made for a manual transmission.<P>Don't you need the actual 3.4 donor car flexplate as it has the proper balancing for the crank?||||reg||1
